Sketchpad, a light pen drawing program for the Type 340
// A light pen drawing program for the Type 340 display, after Ivan Sutherland's Sketchpad. A
// menu bar of light pen labels runs across the top, a tracking target follows the pen through
// the display's pen prediction, and the picture (points, lines, circle arcs, texts, numbers and
// instances of masters, held by constraints, with a truss analysis) is kept as a Type 340
// display list.
// Starts at boot, at 100, which opens the extend window and enters the main bank, bank 4.
// Needs banks 0 to 15, the BBN timesharing clock (IOT 32) for its 1 ms counter, and the Type 550
// Microtape to keep pictures. Includes TYPE340/type340defs.ah, LIGHTPEN/lightpen.ah,
// CLOCK/clockdefs.ah, MICROTAPE/type550defs.ah and TYPE340/trackingTarget.ah; the target's words
// follow trackingTarget.ac's shape. The constants are in sketchpad.ah and the intensities in
// intensities.ah, beside this file.
// Banks. 0 holds the break routine, the frame and every display word but the line slots, which
// alone fill bank 1. 2 holds the arc module, deletion and merging, Define and the master
// directory; 3 the point, line, instance and scalar tables, the dispatch tables and the texts'
// list; 4 the main bank, with the start-up, the main loop, the menus and the modes; 5 Copy's
// store and the constraints' arms' list; 6 the tape module, start-up's gates, the menu census
// and the scale module; 7 the instance module and the menu rows' answers; 8 the constraint
// module; 9 its table, the solver's point tables and the places kept for Undo; 10 the text
// module and the instance table; 11 the truss's analysis, its floating point and the lock's
// display; 12 the break-time helpers, the pen keyboard and the view; 13 the truss's data and
// readouts, the constraints' marks, the line search and the arcs through the view; 14 and 15
// the truss's matrix.
// The code is in the sp*.ac files beside this one, each included where its bank stands, in
// memory order. This file keeps bank 0's variables, the other banks' tables and the bank
// directives.
// The user guide is UsingSketchpad.md and the design SketchpadTechnicalDesign.md, beside this
// file.
//
// 18-Oct-2026 Claude: first release.
// 18-Oct-2026 Claude: production cleanup, comments only.

#include <TYPE340/type340defs.ah>
#include <LIGHTPEN/lightpen.ah>
#include <CLOCK/clockdefs.ah>
#include <MICROTAPE/type550defs.ah>

// The brightness of each kind of thing drawn, the tracking target's among them; before
// trackingTarget.ah, which defaults TARGETINTENSITY only if it is not defined.
#include "intensities.ah"

// Every other constant, and the BOXAT macro, the target's arm and scale among them; before
// trackingTarget.ah, which defaults what is not defined.
#include "sketchpad.ah"
#include <TYPE340/trackingTarget.ah>

// Bank 0's variables, those penISR and the routines beside it use.
// Mailboxes written by penISR, copied and cleared for the main loop by snapshot, with the break
// masked.
// menuArmed is set when a menu hit follows REARM frame ends with none; frameAt is the clock's
// reading at the latest frame end.
var frameTicks, frameAt
var menuHits, menuX, menuY, menuArmed
var tgtHits, tgtX, tgtY

// Kept by penISR from frame to frame, frame ends since the last menu hit, saturating at REARM,
// target presentations since the last target hit, saturating at LOSTMIN, and the clock's
// reading at the last target hit (the main loop also sets it when it restarts the count).
var menuGap, trackMiss, lastHitAt

// Nonzero while the target is displayed; penISR moves the target only then.
var tracking

// Nonzero while a list is open; penISR then posts hits below the bar as menu hits.
var listOpen

// frameGo is where penISR, the watchdog and init start the display, the frame or the pen
// keyboard's list while it is open. kbOn is nonzero while the keyboard is open, when penISR
// posts every hit as a menu hit (spkbd.ac).
var frameGo, kbOn

// Nonzero while the truss's readouts are shown, when penISR starts their list (roList, bank 13)
// at the frame's closing halt. The analysis (sptruss.ac) sets and clears it.
var roOn

// The texts' list to start at the frame's closing halt, before the readouts, 0 for none. It is
// one of the text module's two buffers in bank 3, which its txSync sets.
var txGo

// Nonzero while the constraints' arms are shown, when penISR starts their list (arList, bank 5)
// at the frame's closing halt, before the texts'. The view module's arBegin and arOne set and
// clear it.
var arGo

// Menu hits in the frame being drawn, kept by penISR.
var frameMenuHits

// Diagnostic counters kept by penISR. strayCount counts breaks with no display flag while the
// display runs, lateCount closing halts whose stop flag showed late, and multiFrames frames with
// two or more menu hits.
var edgeCount, strayCount, lateCount, multiFrames

// The main loop's copy of the mailboxes, taken by snapshot.
var sTicks, sFrameAt, sMenuHits, sMenuX, sMenuY, sMenuArmed, sTgtHits, sTgtX, sTgtY

// Target presentations per frame, which penISR counts down.
var callsPerFrame

// An end pair posted by rebuildDisplay for penISR to write, its address (0 when none is
// waiting) and its two words; and bandPost, the arc band's words the arc module posted for
// penISR to write (commitFlip), 0 when none are waiting.
var flipAt, flipW0, flipW1, bandPost

// The target's arms drawn now (tgtKey, clipTarget's key), and a move penISR posted for tgtFlip
// because it changes them (tgtPend set, the new key, and the center's two words). tgtLX and
// tgtLY are the last hit's center words, which penISR has placed or posted; placeTarget clears
// tgtLX, since its move to the middle keeps the arms the last hit left.
var tgtKey, tgtNewKey, tgtPend, tgtPY, tgtPX, tgtLX, tgtLY

// The drawing list, alone in bank 1. Its line slots, target calls and end-of-list jump are all
// written at run time. It is placed ahead of the code so that every reference to it is a
// backward one, which keeps its address literals out of am1's forward-reference pool defect.
// The frame enters it from call0; the line list's end jumps to the arc list in bank 0. The
// 340's subroutine words reach both banks, and a save made here returns here. The CPU only
// stores into it, by full address, from the main bank, whose extend window is open, and from
// bank 2 inside a window. Every bank but 0 is free from its first word.
bank 1
0/
drawList,
    table DRAWLISTSIZE, 0

// The point and line tables in bank 3, with Define's words and the drag's point marks. Ahead of
// the code for the same reason as the drawing list. The main bank and bank 2 reach them through
// a pointer made from their 16-bit address, bank 2 inside an extend window.
bank 3
0/
// Point table, raster coordinates, each axis's table followed by the instances' origins on that
// axis (NVAR words in all). instCount and each instance's master are in bank 10. The tie lists
// follow the scales, so that iScale and iTie are NATT + 1 tables MAXINST apart (instRemove).
pointX,
    table MAXPTS, 0
iX,
    table MAXINST, 0
pointY,
    table MAXPTS, 0
iY,
    table MAXINST, 0

// Line table, point indices.
lineFrom,
    table MAXLINES, 0
lineTo,
    table MAXLINES, 0

// Define's words, before they go into the store.
defBuf,
    table MWORDS, 0

// The points that move with a drag (arcPick, arcDrag, and the instance module's carry,
// instPick), a mark for each, nonzero for a point that moves. Define's map borrows it
// (instMap).
ptMark,
    table MAXPTS, 0

// Each instance's cycle flag, 1 while it cycles (Change > Cycle). It stands before iScale and
// the tie lists, MAXINST apart as they are, so that instRemove moves the three together.
iCyc,
    table MAXINST, 0
iScale,
    table MAXINST, 0
iTie,
    table NATT * MAXINST, 0
// A copy's attachers' points while they merge at its drop, NOPOINT otherwise. Right after the
// tie lists, so that conRen, which renames the tie lists, renames them too.
cpMrg,
    table NATT, NOPOINT
// The designated points, in order, while a copy's attachers merge into them at its drop,
// NOPOINT otherwise. Right after cpMrg, so that conRen renames them too and copyMerge empties
// both together.
desPt,
    table NATT, NOPOINT
// Each canvas text's anchor while it is digits, NOPOINT for a plain text and for every text
// from the text module's txN on. Right after desPt, so that conRen renames them too.
txAn,
    table NTEXT, NOPOINT
// Each canvas text's scalar while it is digits; then the scalars, scN of them, each its value in
// thousandths of an inch and 1 while it is fixed (a value typed). The text module writes them
// through their 16-bit addresses, and the constraint module's D and Y write scVal; the main
// bank's findNearPoint reads scN. txAn to scFix is one run, which a save writes and a load reads
// whole (sptape.ac, TPDIGITS).
txSv,
    table NTEXT, 0
scN, 0
scVal,
    table NSCAL, 0
scFix,
    table NSCAL, 0
// The constraint module's words for the scalars. Each scalar's D's and Y's, counted when the
// sets are built; each scalar's value kept for Undo of an entry (cSnap); and each entry's
// scalar, by its place in the table, NOPOINT for one that names none (cScBind).
scDN,
    table NSCAL, 0
scYN,
    table NSCAL, 0
uScV,
    table NSCAL, 0
cScOf,
    table NCON, NOPOINT

// Three of the main bank's tables, each item's count, a drag's lines and the rebuild's stale
// marks, all reached through a 16-bit address.
// Item number -> times acted on.
itemCount,
    table NITEMS, 0

// Move: the lines on the point being dragged, as line indices.
dragLines,
    table MAXDRAG, 0

// Line indices whose slots the next rebuild writes; staleN of them are in use.
staleList,
    table NSTALE, 0

// The main bank's dispatch tables, the rest of them in spdispatch.ac, included below. The main
// bank reads each through a 16-bit address, its window open, and calls the routine a word names
// by its low 12 bits, in the main bank.
// Where row i's band starts. A hit at or above it, and below row i-1's, is on row i. A
// sublist's rows take the bands from its owning row's on, to row MAXROWS + SUBROWS - 2.
rowThr,
    ROWY0 - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d2 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d3 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d4 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d5 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d6 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d7 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d8 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d9 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d10 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d11 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP
    ROWY0 - 0d12 * ROWPITCH - ROWSLOP

// Bar column -> its action, called via jsp.
barTable,
    actOpen:4           // Draw
    actOpen:4           // Edit
    actOpen:4           // Picture
    actOpen:4           // Misc
    actLocate:4
    actUndo:4
    actStop:4
    actOpen:4           // View

// Item number -> its action, called via jsp once its list has closed.
itemAct,
    actLine:4           // Draw: Line
    actCircle:4         // Draw: Circle
    nothing:4           // Draw: Truss, which owns a sublist
    actText:4           // Draw: Text
    nothing:4           // Draw: Dim, which owns a sublist
    actMove:4           // Edit: Move
    actDelete:4         // Edit: Delete
    nothing:4           // Edit: Constr, which owns a sublist
    nothing:4           // Edit: Size, which owns a sublist
    actScale:4          // Edit: Scale
    nothing:4           // Edit: Change, which owns a sublist
    actDism:4           // Edit: Dismem
    nothing:4           // Picture: Define, which owns a sublist
    nothing:4           // Picture: Inst, which owns a sublist
    nothing:4           // Picture: Copy, which owns a sublist
    actClear:4          // Picture: Clear
    actTie:4            // Picture: Tie
    actDes:4            // Picture: Desig
    actSize:4           // Size: x1
    actSize:4           // Size: x2
    actSize:4           // Size: x4
    actSize:4           // Size: x8
    actInst:4           // Inst: M1
    actInst:4           // Inst: M2
    actInst:4           // Inst: M3
    actInst:4           // Inst: M4
    actCopy:4           // Copy: M1
    actCopy:4           // Copy: M2
    actCopy:4           // Copy: M3
    actCopy:4           // Copy: M4
    actDefine:4         // Define: M1
    actDefine:4         // Define: M2
    actDefine:4         // Define: M3
    actDefine:4         // Define: M4
    actSave:4           // Misc: Save
    actLoad:4           // Misc: Load
    nothing:4           // Misc: Drive, which owns a sublist
    actDir:4            // Misc: Dir
    actDelCons:4        // Misc: Del cons
    actUnfix:4          // Misc: Unfix
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D1
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D2
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D3
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D4
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D5
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D6
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D7
    actDrive:4          // Drive: D8
    actHorv:4           // Constr: Horv
    actCons:4           // Constr: Equal
    actCons:4           // Constr: Paral
    actCons:4           // Constr: Perp
    actCons:4           // Constr: Length
    actCons:4           // Constr: Mid
    actFix:4            // Constr: Fix
    actShow:4           // Constr: Show
    actCons:4           // Truss: Beam
    actCons:4           // Truss: Load
    actRoller:4         // Truss: Roller
    actCons:4           // Truss: Axis
    actForces:4         // Truss: Forces
    actCons:4           // Truss: Stiff
    actChange:4         // Change: M1
    actChange:4         // Change: M2
    actChange:4         // Change: M3
    actChange:4         // Change: M4
    actChange:4         // Change: Cycle
    actCyKb:4           // Change: Dwell
    actCyKb:4           // Change: Seq
    actNumber:4         // Dim: Number
    actCons:4           // Dim: Dist
    actCons:4           // Dim: Change
    actCons:4           // Dim: Gap
    actView:4           // View: x1
    actView:4           // View: x2
    actView:4           // View: x4
    actView:4           // View: x8
    actPan:4            // View: Pan
    actCenter:4         // View: Center

// Constr's rows from ICONS1, Truss's after them, and Dim's Dist, Change and Gap past Change's
// and Number -> the constraint mode's type.
rowCons,
    CTEQ                // Equal
    CTPAR               // Paral
    CTPERP              // Perp
    CTLEN               // Length
    CTMID               // Mid
    0                   // Fix, which has its own action
    0                   // Show, likewise
    CTBEAM              // Truss: Beam
    CTLOAD              // Truss: Load
    0                   // Truss: Roller, which has its own action
    CTROLL              // Truss: Axis, a roller's axis
    0                   // Truss: Forces, which has its own action
    CTSTIFF             // Truss: Stiff, a member's stiffness
    table IDIM + 1 - (ICONS1 + 0d13), 0 // Change's rows and Dim's Number, each its own action
    CTDIST              // Dim: Dist
    CTCHG               // Dim: Change
    CTGAP               // Dim: Gap

// An unused mark block's words, which markUnused copies; markWrite then writes the positions
// and the gates. Each cross is drawn from MARKARM left of its point, right through it, back to
// below it, and up through it.
markTpl,
    scale(DRAWSCALE) intensity(MARKINTENSITY) lpoff next(subroutine)
    jump markEnd:0 next(parameter)
    y(0) next(point)
    x(0) next(vector)
    deltax(2 * MARKARM) deltay(0) right visible
    deltax(MARKARM) deltay(MARKARM) left down
    deltax(0) deltay(2 * MARKARM) up visible end
    lpoff next(point)
    y(0) next(point)
    x(0) next(vector)
    deltax(2 * MARKARM) deltay(0) right visible
    deltax(MARKARM) deltay(MARKARM) left down
    deltax(0) deltay(2 * MARKARM) up visible end
    lpoff next(subroutine)
    jump markEnd:0 next(parameter)
    y(0) next(point)
    x(0) next(vector)
    deltax(2 * MARKARM) deltay(0) right visible
    deltax(MARKARM) deltay(MARKARM) left down
    deltax(0) deltay(2 * MARKARM) up visible end

#include "spdispatch.ac"

// The texts' list, two buffers, each holding per text shown its parameter, y and x words and
// its run, then the halt. The text module (sptext.ac) writes them through their 16-bit
// addresses, and penISR starts the one shown (txGo) after the frame's closing halt; no other
// list is in this bank.
txBufA,
    table TXLISTW, 0
txBufB,
    table TXLISTW, 0

// Each truss joint's unit axis while it is a roller, a_x then a_y, three-word numbers, which the
// truss module (sptruss.ac) writes and reads through its 16-bit address.
taAX,
    table TANJ * 6, 0

// For each truss member, nonzero when an end is a roller on an axis not level (taMI), and its
// Beam parameter word, its stiffness (taMK), which the truss module reaches likewise.
taMI,
    table NCON, 0
taMK,
    table NCON, 0

// Ten of the truss module's three-word numbers (spfloat.ac), which it reaches likewise. The
// pivot being formed and the quotient l of the factorization (taD, taL), 1/L's two inputs (drX,
// drY) and a member's six products (asP1 to asP6, through asPrT and asTab).
taD,
    table 3, 0
taL,
    table 3, 0
drX,
    table 3, 0
drY,
    table 3, 0
asP1,
    table 3, 0
asP2,
    table 3, 0
asP3,
    table 3, 0
asP4,
    table 3, 0
asP5,
    table 3, 0
asP6,
    table 3, 0

// Each instance hidden by the view, nonzero while its figure is not wholly on the screen or
// would pass x8. Written by the instance module's instView, read only while the view is
// magnified, by the lock and the texts' list.
iHid,
    table MAXINST, 0

// Each constraint mark's slot hidden by the view, nonzero while the place it marks is off the
// screen. Written by the marks module's mkMarks for slot j, read by its mkNear, which passes
// over a hidden mark. All 0 at x1.
mkHid,
    table NCON, 0

// Each constraint's rank on its line, for a mark that stands on one: how many entries before it
// in the table name the same line. Counted again by the marks module's mkRanks only when the
// table has changed (mkRkOld, set by bank 8's cBuild), and read by its cMkPos, so that writing
// the marks while points move does not count them again.
mkRank,
    table NCON, 0

// Copy's store, in bank 5 with the constraints' arms' list after it. Master k's points relative
// to its origin from cpX and cpY + k * CPPTS, its lines, indices into those points, from cpFrom
// and cpTo + k * CPLINES, and its arcs as the arc table holds them, from cpC to cpK + k *
// CPARCS. Written by Define in bank 2 and read by Copy in the main bank and bank 2, through
// 16-bit addresses. Ahead of the code for the same reason as the drawing list.
bank 5
0/
cpX,
    table NMASTER * CPPTS, 0
cpY,
    table NMASTER * CPPTS, 0
cpFrom,
    table NMASTER * CPLINES, 0
cpTo,
    table NMASTER * CPLINES, 0
cpC,
    table NMASTER * CPARCS, 0
cpS,
    table NMASTER * CPARCS, 0
cpE,
    table NMASTER * CPARCS, 0
cpD,
    table NMASTER * CPARCS, 0
cpK,
    table NMASTER * CPARCS, 0
// Master k's attachers, their master point indices in designation order from cpAtt + k * NATT,
// cpNAtt + k of them. After cpK, so that the tape's run of the store takes them with it.
cpAtt,
    table NMASTER * NATT, 0
cpNAtt,
    table NMASTER, 0
// The constraints' arms' list, after the store and outside the tape's run of it. A display list
// that penISR starts by dla after the frame's closing halt while arGo is set, since the 340
// jumps only within banks 0 and 1, and which ends in a halt. NCON slots of ARMWORDS, packed,
// slot k the k-th E, P or R entry in the table, and the word after the last used, its parameter
// word's place, the halt. The view module's arBegin and arOne (bank 12) write it, through
// 16-bit addresses. Assembled empty.
arList,
    lpoff halt interrupt
    table NCON * ARMWORDS, 0
    lpoff halt interrupt
    halt

// arcKeep's save of the arc module's words arcCX to arcQY (bank 2, spedit.ac), which arcKeep
// reaches inside an extend window.
akSave,
    table AKEEPN, 0
bank 0

#include "spbreak.ac"

#include "spframe.ac"

variables
constants

// The main bank holds the start-up, the main loop, the menus, the mode handlers and the drawing
// list's upkeep, with their variables; their tables are in bank 3, and the instance code is bank
// 7's module, entered only through instCall. It runs with the extend window open, so a reference to
// a word in bank 0 (penISR's variables, the display) is made through its 16-bit address,
// OP i [X:0], and one to a table in bank 3 through a pointer made from [X:3]. It is placed
// after banks 0 and 3, so that every reference it makes to them is a backward one.
bank 4
0/
#include "spmain.ac"

#include "spmenus.ac"

#include "spundo.ac"

#include "spmodes.ac"

#include "sppen.ac"

#include "spdisplay.ac"

variables
constants

// The arc module, alone in bank 2. It holds the arcs' geometry, their table, and the words of
// their slots and of the arc band in bank 0; and, since arcs hang on points, the routines that
// remove points and lines, merge and delete; and Define and the master directory, and Copy's
// store and its arcs; the main bank takes a copy's points and lines from the store itself. The
// main bank enters it only through arcCall, with an entry number
// (AEINIT to AEUNDO), and reads Define's words through their 16-bit address; the module runs
// with the extend window closed, opening it only to read the variables of the main bank and
// bank 0 and the tables of banks 3, 5 and 8 and to store into them or the display lists, and it
// calls nothing outside bank 2 but bank 12's lineArc, loadLine and vwCross and bank 13's vaSlot
// and vaBand, each by jsp i [X:01n]. It is placed after banks 0 and 4, so that every reference
// it makes to them is a backward one.
// Vertex k of an arc is its start rotated k steps of 2pi/NARC about the center, worked out
// directly from the start with a quarter-wave table of sines, so no error builds up from step
// to step and a full circle closes exactly on its start. Offsets from the center are kept in
// 32nds of a unit, rounded to a unit only for the display. An arc slot's vectors run the full
// circle backward, from vertex NARC down to vertex 0, the start; only the last carries end. The
// gate enters the last k of them for an arc of k whole steps, or the word before those, which
// then holds the part step from the end to vertex k.
bank 2
0/

#include "sparcs.ac"

#include "spedit.ac"

#include "spdrag.ac"

#include "spdefine.ac"

#include "sparcdata.ac"

constants

// The tape module, in bank 6. It moves a picture to or from the Microtape, with the display on
// WAIT (waitList) and the break system off, and keeps the tape's directory and its screen. The
// main bank enters it through tapeCall, with an entry number (TESAVE to TEDIR), and at
// tpPickName for Save's name; it runs with the extend window open, reaching the picture's words
// in banks 0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9 and 10 through 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside bank
// 6 but the view module's vwInit. It is placed after the banks it reaches, so that every
// reference it makes to them is a backward one. After it, start-up's gates (spinit.ac's
// initGates), run once between bank 12's initVars and the main bank's init. Then the menu's
// census (spcensus.ac), which the main bank's actOpen takes as a list opens. Then the scale
// module (spscale.ac), Edit > Scale and its mode, entered by the main bank's gates.
bank 6
0/

#include "sptape.ac"

#include "spinit.ac"

#include "spcensus.ac"

#include "spscale.ac"

constants

// The instance module, in bank 7. It keeps the instance list's slots in bank 0, and adds,
// places, moves, locks, sizes and removes an instance. The main bank enters it only through
// instCall, with an entry number
// (IEINIT to IEVIEW; the view module enters it too, for IEVIEW), and writes litInst at init
// through its 16-bit address; it runs with the extend window open, reaching the main bank's
// variables, the master directory in bank 2 and the instance tables in banks 3 and 10 through
// 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside bank 7 but the text module's entries for it (bank
// 10) and the view module's vwBox (bank 12), as spinst.ac's header says. It is placed last, so
// that every reference it makes to the other banks is a backward one. After it, which menu
// rows can act (sprows.ac's rowCan), entered by the main bank's menus directly, from the census
// in bank 6.
bank 7
0/

#include "spinst.ac"

#include "sprows.ac"

// arcFill's kept offsets (bank 2), vertices 0 to NQ-1 of the circle it fills, each v then u.
arcOff,
    table 2*NQ, 0

constants

// The constraint module's tables, alone in bank 9, the places it keeps for Undo and the point
// tables it works on. The module reaches them through their 16-bit addresses, and bank 2's
// ptMarked and the main bank's conRedraw read cFlag so. Placed before bank 8, so that every
// reference the module makes to them is a backward one. Each point table has a word for each of
// the solver's variables (NVAR), the points' and then the instances' origins'.
bank 0d9
0/

// Every point's place when an entry was added (cSnap), read back by cUndo.
uSX,
    table NVAR, 0
uSY,
    table NVAR, 0

// Each point's flags: FIN while it is the solver's, FFIX while it is fixed, FMOV while it is
// moved by the last publish (cPublish) or put back by Undo (cUndo), and FTCH while this pass's
// sweeps have touched it (cTouch). Bank 2's ptMarked reads FMOV in place of ptMark while the arc
// module works out the arcs on the moved points (conArcs), and conRedraw reads it.
cFlag,
    table NVAR, 0

// The points this pass's sweeps touched, once each, in the order touched (cTouch); cPublish
// then compacts the ones it moved to the front, cMovN of them, which carry the FMOV marks, and
// so do the points Undo put back (cUndo). The next pass clears the marks from the front alone
// (cUnmark).
cPub,
    table NVAR, 0

// The working values, in 32nds of a unit, of the solver's points.
wX,
    table NVAR, 0
wY,
    table NVAR, 0

// Where the last publish found each point it moved, or Undo each point it put back, for
// cRevert.
oX,
    table NVAR, 0
oY,
    table NVAR, 0

// The solver's points (cBuild).
cIn,
    table NVAR, 0

// The ties the solver keeps (cBuild), each tie's place in the tie lists, a * MAXINST + i.
cTies,
    table NATT * MAXINST, 0

// Each entry's lines' lengths, in 32nds, as the last sweep found or set them, two words an entry
// by its place in the table (line A-B's, then line C-D's). An E's or an L's root starts from them
// (cProjM). A place another entry has taken since only costs that root more steps (cHyp). A C
// entry keeps its circle's radius in its first word likewise (cProjK, cRim).
cLast,
    table NCON * 2, 0

// Each arc's radius, in 32nds, as its implicit C last brought its ends to it, by the arc's index:
// both rays' roots start from it (cProjC, cRim). An arc replaced or renumbered
// since only costs those roots more steps (cHyp).
cArcG,
    table MAXARCS, 0

// The lines on the solver's points (cBuild), which the main bank's conRedraw reads too.
cLines,
    table MAXLINES, 0

// The masters' constraints, master k's from cpCon + k * NCPCON * CW, CW words each as
// the table holds them but in master point indices, cpNCon + k of them. Written by Define (the
// instance module's instDef), read by Copy's drop (cCopy), and saved with each picture
// (sptape.ac).
cpCon,
    table NMASTER * NCPCON * CW, 0
cpNCon,
    table NMASTER, 0

// The arcs the solver keeps (cBuild); cKeep's slots, a line, a second line and an arc each; and
// per constraint type, indexed by the type word's low bits (CTMASK), how many points it names
// (A, A and B, A to C, or A to D).
cArcs,
    table MAXARCS, 0
kpLock,
    table 0d9, 0
cNPts,
    0
    2                   // CTHL
    2                   // CTHP
    1                   // CTF
    4                   // CTEQ
    2                   // CTLEN
    4                   // CTPAR
    4                   // CTPERP
    3                   // CTMID
    3                   // CTON
    3                   // CTONC
    1                   // CTATT
    2                   // CTBEAM
    2                   // CTLOAD
    3                   // CTROLL: its point, then its axis's line
    1                   // CTDES
    3                   // CTDIST: line A-B, then the digits' anchor
    3                   // CTCHG: likewise
    2                   // CTGAP: its point, then the digits' anchor

// Per type, indexed likewise, the mark's call of its glyph; a designation's mark calls instead
// the digit for its place in the order, from cDgTab, designation 1 first (cMarks).
cGlyph,
    0
    save gH:0 next(subroutine)
    save gH:0 next(subroutine)
    save gF:0 next(subroutine)
    save gE:0 next(subroutine)
    save gL:0 next(subroutine)
    save gP:0 next(subroutine)
    save gR:0 next(subroutine)
    save gX:0 next(subroutine)
    save gN:0 next(subroutine)
    save gC:0 next(subroutine)
    save gA:0 next(subroutine)
    save gB:0 next(subroutine)
    save gW:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO0:0 next(subroutine)  // a roller's mark is cRlTab's instead (cMarks)
    save gD1:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD:0 next(subroutine)
    save gY:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO:0 next(subroutine)
cDgTab,
    save gD1:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD2:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD3:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD4:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD5:0 next(subroutine)
    save gD6:0 next(subroutine)

// A roller's mark by its axis's direction, k * 22.5 degrees counterclockwise from level, k 0 to 7
// (cRlDir).
cRlTab,
    save gO0:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO1:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO2:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO3:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO4:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO5:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO6:0 next(subroutine)
    save gO7:0 next(subroutine)

// A mark on one line stands beside it (cMkPos). Per type, indexed like cNPts, where the entry
// names its line, 1 when in words 1 and 2 (H, L, a Beam's B, a Load's W), 2 when in words 2 and
// 3 after its point (X, N), 0 for a mark not on one line.
cLnTab,
    0
    1                   // CTHL
    1                   // CTHP
    0                   // CTF
    0                   // CTEQ
    1                   // CTLEN
    0                   // CTPAR
    0                   // CTPERP
    2                   // CTMID
    2                   // CTON
    0                   // CTONC
    0                   // CTATT
    1                   // CTBEAM
    1                   // CTLOAD
    0                   // CTROLL
    0                   // CTDES
    0                   // CTDIST
    0                   // CTCHG
    0                   // CTGAP

// Per direction k (cRlDir: k * 22.5 degrees from level), the direction of the mark's offset
// from its place on the line, x then y, at right angles to it, in thousandths of the distance
// (cMkPos scales it, quantizing once). Above a flat line (k 0 to 2, 6, 7), right of a steep one
// (k 3 to 5), as the truss's readouts stand. The cosines and sines of 0, 22.5, 45 and 67.5
// degrees.
cOfX,
    0
    -0d383
    -0d707
    0d924
    0d1000
    0d924
    0d707
    0d383
cOfY,
    0d1000
    0d924
    0d707
    -0d383
    0
    0d383
    0d707
    0d924

// The constraint table, conTab (spcons.ac's header describes it), cCount, then NCON entries
// of CW words.
conTab,
cCount, 0
cEntries,
    table NCON * CW, 0

constants

// The constraint module, alone in bank 8, the solver and the sets it works on; its table and
// point tables are in bank 9. The main bank enters it only through conCall, with an entry
// number (CEINIT to CESTSET); it runs with the extend window open, reaching the point, line and
// arc tables, the main bank's variables and its tables in bank 9 through 16-bit addresses, and
// calls nothing outside bank 8 but the marks in bank 13 (spmarks.ac). Bank 2, the main bank and
// the tape module reach its table and words through their 16-bit addresses. It is placed last,
// so that every reference it makes to the other banks is a backward one.
bank 0d8
0/

#include "spcons.ac"

constants

// The text module, in bank 10 with its tables. The main bank enters it through txCall, the
// instance module and initVars at its entries, by their 16-bit addresses; its list is in bank 3.
bank 0d10
0/

#include "sptext.ac"

// The instance table, instCount instances, each its master; their origins, scales and ties are
// in bank 3. Every user reaches it through its 16-bit address.
instCount, 0
iMaster,
    table MAXINST, 0

constants

// The truss's analysis, in bank 11, the members' forces, a slice a pass, and the readouts,
// whose list is in bank 13; then its floating point (spfloat.ac).
// The main bank enters it at taInit and taTick; it runs with the extend window open, reaching
// the constraint table, the point table, the main bank's words, bank 0's and banks 14 and 15's
// through 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside bank 11. Placed after the banks it
// reaches but 14 and 15, which hold only reserved words. Then the display of what a lift will
// take (splock.ac); the main bank enters it through showDot and the entries its header names,
// and it calls nothing outside banks 11 and 12.
bank 0d11
0/

#include "sptruss.ac"
#include "spfloat.ac"
#include "splock.ac"

constants

// Bank 12 holds the copy of penISR's mailboxes for the main loop (snapshot), the writes made
// between frames (commitFlip and tgtFlip) and the lock mark's arms (clipLock). None is reached
// by the display. Each runs with the extend window open, reaching bank 0's and the main bank's
// words through 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside bank 12. Placed last, so that every
// reference it makes to the other banks is a backward one. Then the pen keyboard (spkbd.ac),
// entered the same way, with its list and the directory's, which penISR starts by full address.
// Then the view module (spview.ac), entered the same way.
bank 0d12
0/

#include "spaux.ac"
#include "spkbd.ac"
#include "spview.ac"

constants

// Bank 13's data. The truss's snapshot, which taCheck (sptruss.ac) compares and writes through
// 16-bit addresses. Reached the same way, the incidences, whose words hold the map until the
// analysis's directions pass writes them (taInc, taMap), and each member's coefficients on its
// ends' horizontal or axis unknowns (tdC, A's then B's); the rollers' axes, taAX, and the
// members' taMI and taMK are in bank 3. Then the readouts' list (roList), which penISR starts by
// full address, per readout a parameter, a y and an x word and at most three of characters, one
// for each entry at most, then UNSTABLE's six words and the halt.
bank 0d13
0/

taSnap,
    table NCON * 0d8, 0
taInc,
taMap,
    table MAXPTS, 0
tdC,
    table NCON * 6, 0
roList,
    table NCON * 6 + 7, 0

// After the data, the constraints' marks (spmarks.ac). The constraint module enters them at
// mkMarks and mkNear by their 16-bit addresses; they run with the extend window open, reaching
// bank 8's words, the constraint table and bank 0's fixList through 16-bit addresses, and call
// nothing outside bank 13.
#include "spmarks.ac"

// Then the line search, which finds the nearest line to the target's center, and in Line,
// Circle and Move the second nearest and the two lines' crossing, swept a slice a pass. The
// main bank's placeLock
// enters it at lineSearch; it runs with the extend window open, reaching the point and line
// tables and the main bank's variables through 16-bit addresses, and calls nothing outside bank
// 13. Placed after the banks it reaches, so that every reference it makes to them is a backward
// one.
#include "spsearch.ac"

// Then the arcs through the magnifier's view (spvarc.ac). The arc module enters it at vaSlot
// and vaBand by their 16-bit addresses; it runs with the extend window
// open, reaching the arc module's words, the slots and bank 12's view module through 16-bit
// addresses, and calls nothing outside banks 12 and 13 (the clipper, through vwClipX).
#include "spvarc.ac"

constants

// The truss's direct solve, banks 14 and 15, data only, reached by sptruss.ac through 16-bit
// addresses and written before each is read, so not on the tape. Per unknown its
// row's base address and first coupled unknown (tdU), 1/D (tdRD) and the right side, then the
// displacements (tdY); per member e_x and e_y (tdE); then the matrix's profile, run on through
// bank 15 (tdK, tdK2). Numbers are three words (spfloat.ac).
bank 0d14
0/

tdU,
    table TANU * 2
tdRD,
    table TANU * 3
tdY,
    table TANU * 3
tdE,
    table NCON * 6
tdK,
    table 0d4096 - TANU * 0d8 - NCON * 6

bank 0d15
0/

tdK2,
    table 0d4096

bank 0
start boot
